# madcide default theme = JOE parity (owner directive 2026-08-26: match
# what joe shows). Mapping observed from joe 4.6's own default scheme
# (/usr/share/joe/colors/default.jcf + syntax/c.jsf class inheritance):
# Comment=green; Constant=cyan (c.jsf: Number and String both inherit
# +Constant); Keyword=bold; Type=bold; idents plain — so `function`
# stays unthemed here (JOE has no function class; our AST-backed one is
# an ADDITION, styled in the vivid/classic schemes). JOE classes we do
# not classify yet (Preproc blue, Brace magenta, Escape bold cyan, Bad
# bold red) are named classifier seats in the JOE look/feel recon doc.
# One class + spec per line (JOE's spec vocabulary; ^K T swaps schemes).
keyword bold
type bold
string cyan
number cyan
comment green

# @gui (slice 3): the web target's workbench colours/fonts as CSS custom
# properties (the @scope rule; the TUI ignores these). One file, two
# renderings. A property left out keeps the page's default.
@gui bg #1b1d24
@gui fg #d9dbe4
@gui accent #7aa2f7

# @presence (client-server V3c): the caret colours dealt round-robin to
# clients at connect (a slot per line; the window renders another client's
# caret in its slot colour, the TUI ignores these). Eight distinguishable
# entries over the sixteen-colour palette (bold = bright).
@presence 0 cyan
@presence 1 magenta
@presence 2 yellow
@presence 3 green
@presence 4 red
@presence 5 blue
@presence 6 bold cyan
@presence 7 bold magenta
